{% comment %}
=====================================================================
 One document per issue — the smallest useful report
 ---------------------------------------------------------------------
 Set the template's OUTPUT to "One document per issue" and its SOURCE to
 "Issues". Every issue in the selected query then produces one PDF page
 (or one page per issue in the combined download).

 Inside a per-issue template the variable is `issue`. The sidebar beside
 the editor lists everything it can print, with a copyable snippet for
 each accessor — that list is read from the code itself, so it cannot
 tell you about a field that no longer exists.

 THE THREE CLASSES USED BELOW ARE THIS PLUGIN'S ONLY PUBLIC ONES:

   .rrd-card    a block that is never split across a page break
   .rrd-number  right-aligned, with figures that line up in a column
   .rrd-muted   smaller, quieter text

 Everything else is styled by the report stylesheet, which is the same
 one the HTML preview and the PDF use — so what you see in the preview
 is what the PDF has, at a different size.
=====================================================================
{% endcomment %}

<h1>{{ issue.tracker }} #{{ issue.id }}</h1>
<p class="rrd-muted">{{ issue.project.name }} · {{ issue.status }} · {{ issue.priority }}</p>

<div class="rrd-card">
  <table>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <th>Author</th>
        <td>{{ issue.author.name }}</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th>Assignee</th>
        {% comment %} An unassigned issue prints an em dash rather than an empty cell, so a
           reader can tell "nobody" from "the report lost it". {% endcomment %}
        <td>{% if issue.assignee %}{{ issue.assignee.name }}{% else %}—{% endif %}</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th>Target version</th>
        <td>{% if issue.version %}{{ issue.version }}{% else %}—{% endif %}</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th>Start / due</th>
        <td>{{ issue.start_date }} → {{ issue.due_date }}</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th>Estimated</th>
        <td class="rrd-number">{{ issue.estimated_hours }} h</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        {% comment %} `spent_hours` is a BATCH accessor: reading it for every issue in a
           report costs one query for the whole run rather than one per issue. The sidebar
           marks the accessors that behave this way. It also shows only the hours the
           report's own reader is allowed to see. {% endcomment %}
        <th>Spent</th>
        <td class="rrd-number">{{ issue.spent_hours }} h</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <th>Done</th>
        <td class="rrd-number">{{ issue.done_ratio }} %</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</div>

<h2>{{ issue.subject }}</h2>

{% comment %} `| escape` is not needed on a value this plugin renders into HTML — every
   interpolation is escaped already. It IS needed inside a <script>, where `| json` is the
   filter to use; the linter beside this editor says so if you forget. {% endcomment %}
<div class="rrd-card">
  {{ issue.description }}
</div>

<p class="rrd-muted">
  <a href="{{ issue.url }}">{{ issue.url }}</a>
</p>
